column5:
add subplot in:
def plot_shoeGearContactInfo(self, tmin = -1, tmax = -1):
purpose is to plot the relative position, velocity of a single contact point that is tracked

Add utility free functions for reading Chrono::Vehicle subsystems from JSON specification files.

- all these functions are implemented in ChUtilsJSON.{h,cpp}
- eliminate code duplication in member functions

Add support for marking entities as "deprecated".

- the macro `CH_DEPRECATED` (defined in ChPlatform.h) generates warnings at compile time including an optional message.
- usage:
      For typedef:         typedef CH_DEPRECATED int test1;
      For classes/structs: class CH_DEPRECATED test2 { ... };
      For methods:         class test3 { CH_DEPRECATED virtual void foo() {} };
      For functions:       template<class T> CH_DEPRECATED void test4() {}
- users can disable these warnings by defining `CH_IGNORE_DEPRECATED`
- when building the Chrono libraries, CH_IGNORE_DEPRECATED is always defined (in the corresponding CMakeLists.txt files) to stop issuing these warnings during the library compilation.

OpenMP: only include omp.h in files calling the omp api

#include <omp.h> is only required in files calling omp_* functions
It is not required in files only using #pragma omp

Automatically invoke SetupInitial.

- use the is_initialized flag to automatically trigger a call to ChSystem::SetupInitial (if needed);
- this check is performed in the various ChSystem::Do*** analysis functions, as well as in ChSystem::Update (for situations were Update is called by the user);
- all SetupInitial functions were marked as private;
- removed calls to SetupInitial from all demos and tests

Improved the computational performance a lot:
 - removed the intermediate redundant matrices;
 - changed some remaining intermediate matrices from dense to sparse;
 - replaced the heavy transformation matrix multiplications by the coordinate transforamtions for sub-blocks.

Matlab utility function to load the data "solve_nnnn_mm_M.dat"  that has been dumped to file by the ChSystem  at each nnnn step and mm sub-solve in step (same for Cq, M, E, matrices etc.)
Use for instance as
   [ M, Cq, E,  R, Qc, Dv, L] = load_system_matrices(framenumber, solvenumber, directory);
   spy( [M, Cq'; Cq, E] );
where directory is optional (looks in working directory).

fixed a few modeling bugs.
Kinematic tests PASSED for a few seconds (>10) of simulation time.
  double tol_pos = 1e-6;
  double tol_vel = 1e-4;
  double tol_acc = 1e-3;
Infinity norm of the difference between the wheel states of the two systems compared to tolerances.

Fix bugs in initialization of the ChSolidAxle suspension:

- Fix incorrect coordinate system for initialization of the revolute joint between spindle and upright (the chassis rotation was not taken into account);
- Fix calculation of the end points of the axle body for visualization.

Use free function utilities for loading JSON arrays.

- Eliminate code duplication
- Implemented in ChUtilsJSON.{h,cpp}

Improvement on modal assembly:
 - Extended to constrained subsystems with internal-internal fixed links, internal-boundary fixed links, and boundary-boundary links;
 - Implemented the static correction mode when external forces are imposed on the internal bodies and nodes;
 - Refactored pieces of code and renamed some variables and functions;
 - Other minor improvements.

Always re-calculate matrix dimension in ChSolverDirect::Setup.

- this is needed to accommodate possible system changes (e.g. addition/deletion of physics elements) and is separate from the issue of forcing an update of the sparsity pattern learner;
- also eliminated an unecessary call to UpdateCountsAndOffsets in ChSystem::Integrate_Y

Add mechanism to selectively disable/enable collision for subsystems.

This is based on an enum (TrackCollide::Enum), currently defined in ChTrackedVehicle.h which contains bit flags that can be combined with bit operations.  For example, to only enable collision for the right road wheels and the right track shoes, use:
my_vehicle.SetCollide(TrackCollide::WHEELS_RIGHT | TrackCollide::SHOES_RIGHT);

optionally get sparsity pattern before building CSR matrix

to enable feature, before running simulation, call:
mkl_solver->SetSparsityPatternLock(true);
mkl_solver->ForceSparsityPatternUpdate();
(order is irrelevant)
Use to avoid slowdown at first step when ChSolverMKL is used with ChCSR3Matrix.
To eventually re-update the sparsity pattern just call again
mkl_solver->ForceSparsityPatternUpdate();

Rename collision files and classes:

- rename ChModelBullet to ChCollisionModelBullet
- rename all ChC***.{cpp,h} files to ChCollision***.{cpp,h}

Place all classes in Chrono::Irrlicht under the namespace `chrono::irrlicht`.

All demo and test programs that use the Chrono::Irrlicht module must be modified accordingly.  The easiest way is to simply add the following using statement:
using namespace chrono::irrlicht;

Removed overabundant constraints on Abaqus INP file loader ChMeshFileLoader::FromAbaqusInput (backward compatible)

- elements were asked to be inserted with ascending IDs, but this is not required by Abaqus Reference, thus it has been removed;
- elements and node linkage was depending on the order of insertion in the std::vector, now it is based on the node ID, according to the INP file itself;
- nodes IDs order is not checked; it is enough that the nodes of the element have been previously loaded;
- Abaqus INP is case-insensitive, so does the FromAbaqusInput loader

#include "render.h"

class System {
public:
	System(int cudaDevice);
	~System() {
	}
	void Setup();
	void SetTimingFile(string fname);

	double GetKE();
	double GetMFR(double height);
	void DoTimeStep();
	void PrintStats();
	void InitObject(ChSharedPtr<CHBODY> &body, double mass, ChVector<> pos, ChQuaternion<> rot, double sfric, double kfric, double restitution, bool collide, bool fixed, int family, int nocolwith);
	void AddCollisionGeometry(ChSharedPtr<CHBODY> &body, ShapeType type, ChVector<> dim, ChVector<> lPos, ChQuaternion<> lRot);
	void FinalizeObject(ChSharedPtr<CHBODY> body);
	void DeactivationPlane(float y, float h, bool disable);
	void BoundingPlane(float y);
